Contexto documental indexado:
[FONTE 1]
Referência: [Fonte: Declaring Auto-configurations in Spring Boot 3.x (https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/reference/features/developing-auto-configuration.html)]
Módulo: core (Spring Boot 3.4.0)
Conteúdo:
In Spring Boot 3.x, auto-configuration classes must be declared in:
`META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports`

The legacy file `META-INF/spring.factories` is no longer supported for auto-configuration registration in Spring Boot 3.x.

```java
package com.example.demo.autoconfigure;

import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.condition.ConditionalOnClass;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.condition.ConditionalOnMissingBean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;

@AutoConfiguration
@ConditionalOnClass(DataSource.class)
public class CustomDatabaseAutoConfiguration {

    @Bean
    @ConditionalOnMissingBean
    public CustomDatabaseService databaseService() {
        return new CustomDatabaseService();
    }
}
```


Pergunta do desenvolvedor:
Onde devem ser declaradas as classes de auto-configuração no Spring Boot 3.x?

Resposta técnica fundamentada exclusivamente no contexto acima (incluindo citações):

No Spring Boot 3.x, as classes de auto-configuração devem ser declaradas no arquivo:
`META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports`

O arquivo legado `META-INF/spring.factories` não é mais suportado para registro de auto-configurações no Spring Boot 3.x.

Exemplo com anotação `@AutoConfiguration`:
```java
package com.example.demo.autoconfigure;

import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.condition.ConditionalOnClass;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.condition.ConditionalOnMissingBean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;

@AutoConfiguration
@ConditionalOnClass(DataSource.class)
public class CustomDatabaseAutoConfiguration {

    @Bean
    @ConditionalOnMissingBean
    public CustomDatabaseService databaseService() {
        return new CustomDatabaseService();
    }
}
```

[Fonte: Declaring Auto-configurations in Spring Boot 3.x (https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/reference/features/developing-auto-configuration.html)]
